{%- comment -%}
  Full instructor roster — one paginated grid, read straight from the
  metaobject definition.

  REPLACES the two-metafield repeater arrangement on
  templates/page.instructors-list.json:

    before   page "our-team"
             ├─ custom.our_team    list.metaobject_reference → 50 refs → section A
             └─ custom.our_team_2  list.metaobject_reference → 22 refs → section B

    after    shop.metaobjects.our_team.values → 72 → this one section

  Nothing migrates. The 72 entries are already shop-scoped — a metaobject
  definition always is. What the page metafields held was a pointer LIST, and
  that pointer layer is what goes away. The split into two fields existed only
  because looping a list metafield silently stops at 50.

  WHY {% paginate %} WHEN 72 < 250
  A bare loop over .values stops at 50 with no error — instructor 51 through
  72 would simply not be on the page, and nothing would tell you. {% paginate %}
  is officially supported on metaobject_definition.values and takes a page size
  up to 250, so at 72 entries the wrapper lifts the cap and the pagination UI
  never renders. It stays dormant until entry 251.

  Loop the EXPRESSION, not a copy made before the block opens — an assign that
  reads .values above {% paginate %} captures the unpaginated 50-item array.
  Assigns INSIDE the block are fine, which is where the sort/filter happen.

  WHAT THIS SECTION CANNOT DO THAT THE METAFIELD LISTS COULD
  1. Manual ordering. A list metafield is a hand-sorted array. .values is not.
     Ordering needs a real field on the definition — see `sort_by` below.
  2. Act as a publish gate. Previously an instructor appeared because someone
     added the reference. Here EVERY entry appears unless filtered — see
     `visible_field`. Both default to off so this section behaves identically
     to the old one until those fields actually exist.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'instructor.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- if section.settings.enable_filter -%}
  <script src="{{ 'instructor-filter.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The type handle is HARDCODED, not a setting.

  {% paginate %} requires a static path. Passing a bracket lookup built from a
  variable -- shop.metaobjects[handle].values -- fails outright with
  "Array ... is not paginateable". A theme setting therefore cannot drive it.
  Changing the roster type means editing this file, which is honest: the
  alternative is a setting that silently does nothing.

  club-instructors keeps its metaobject_type setting because it does NOT
  paginate -- bracket lookups are fine everywhere except the paginate tag.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign all_entries = shop.metaobjects.our_team.values -%}

<div class="club-roster color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} gradient">
  <div class="page-width">
    {%- comment -%}
      h2, not h1. The <h1> on a page template belongs to main-page, which
      renders {{ page.title }} -- the title set in admin. Two h1s is the
      "double title" symptom: one from main-page, one from here.

      Leave this heading BLANK when the admin page title already says it.
      Fill it in only when the section needs a label distinct from the page
      title, e.g. page title "教练团队" + section heading "认证教练".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <div class="club-roster__head">
        <h2 class="club-roster__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
          <p class="club-roster__sub">{{ section.settings.subheading }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if all_entries == blank or all_entries.size == 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A wrong type handle resolves to nil and renders nothing, silently.
        Say so in the editor; storefront visitors get nothing rather than a
        broken-looking diagnostic.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        <p class="club-roster__empty">
          No metaobject type named <code>our_team</code>, or it has no entries.
          Check the API handle under Settings › Custom data › Metaobjects — the
          handle, not the display name. Also confirm the definition is exposed
          to storefronts, or <code>shop.metaobjects</code> cannot see it.
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- paginate shop.metaobjects.our_team.values by section.settings.per_page -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Re-read the EXPRESSION inside the block. The assign made above the
          paginate tag is used only for the existence check and the total
          count, never for iteration — an assign created before the block
          opens captures the unpaginated 50-item array.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign roster = shop.metaobjects.our_team.values -%}

        {%- if section.settings.visible_field != blank -%}
          {%- assign roster = roster | where: section.settings.visible_field, true -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.sort_by != blank -%}
          {%- assign roster = roster | sort: section.settings.sort_by -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if request.design_mode -%}
          <p class="club-roster__count">
            Showing {{ roster.size }} of {{ all_entries.size }} entries.
            (Editor only — visitors do not see this.)
          </p>
          {%- if section.settings.enable_filter and paginate.pages > 1 -%}
            <p class="club-roster__empty">
              WARNING: the roster is split across {{ paginate.pages }} pages, but
              filtering is client-side — it can only filter the cards on the
              current page while appearing to search everything. Raise “Entries
              per page”, or turn filtering off until this becomes a server-side
              filter.
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- liquid
          assign f1 = section.settings.facet_1_field
          assign f2 = section.settings.facet_2_field
          assign search_label = 'sections.instructors.search_label' | t

          assign facet_1_label = section.settings.facet_1_label
          if facet_1_label == blank
            case f1
              when 'certification'
                assign facet_1_label = 'sections.instructors.facets.certification' | t
              when 'type'
                assign facet_1_label = 'sections.instructors.facets.type' | t
              when 'client_groups'
                assign facet_1_label = 'sections.instructors.facets.client_groups' | t
            endcase
          endif

          assign facet_2_label = section.settings.facet_2_label
          if facet_2_label == blank
            case f2
              when 'certification'
                assign facet_2_label = 'sections.instructors.facets.certification' | t
              when 'type'
                assign facet_2_label = 'sections.instructors.facets.type' | t
              when 'client_groups'
                assign facet_2_label = 'sections.instructors.facets.client_groups' | t
            endcase
          endif
        -%}

        <instructor-filter>
          {%- if section.settings.enable_filter -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              no-js-hidden: with JS off the controls never appear and the full
              roster renders. A visible control that does nothing is worse than
              no control.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="club-filter no-js-hidden" role="search" aria-label="{{ search_label | escape }}">
              {%- if section.settings.filter_by_name -%}
                <div class="club-filter__search field">
                  <input
                    id="InstructorSearch-{{ section.id }}"
                    type="search"
                    class="club-filter__input field__input"
                    placeholder="{{ search_label | escape }}"
                    autocomplete="off"
                    enterkeyhint="search"
                    data-instructor-search
                  >
                  <label class="field__label" for="InstructorSearch-{{ section.id }}">
                    {{- search_label -}}
                  </label>
                  <span class="club-filter__search-icon field__button" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg class="icon icon-search" viewBox="0 0 18 19" fill="none" focusable="false">
                      <path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M11.03 11.68A5.784 5.784 0 112.85 3.5a5.784 5.784 0 018.18 8.18zm.26 1.12a6.78 6.78 0 11.72-.7l5.4 5.4a.5.5 0 11-.71.7l-5.41-5.4z" fill="currentColor"/>
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if f1 != blank -%}
                <fieldset class="club-filter__group" hidden data-facet-group="1">
                  <legend class="club-filter__legend">{{ facet_1_label }}</legend>
                </fieldset>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if f2 != blank -%}
                <fieldset class="club-filter__group" hidden data-facet-group="2">
                  <legend class="club-filter__legend">{{ facet_2_label }}</legend>
                </fieldset>
              {%- endif -%}

              <div class="club-filter__status">
                <p
                  class="club-filter__count"
                  role="status"
                  aria-live="polite"
                  data-instructor-count
                  data-template="{{ 'sections.instructors.count' | t: shown: '[shown]', total: '[total]' | escape }}"
                ></p>
                <button type="button" class="club-filter__clear link" hidden data-instructor-clear>
                  {{- 'sections.instructors.clear' | t -}}
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="club-roster__empty" hidden data-instructor-empty>
              {{ 'sections.instructors.no_results' | t }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

        <ul
          class="club-roster__grid list-unstyled"
          style="--roster-columns: {{ section.settings.columns }};"
          role="list"
        >
          {%- for entry in roster -%}
            {%- liquid
              # Never write a percent-brace sequence inside this tag body,
              # not even in a comment line. The tokenizer closes the tag at
              # the first closing delimiter it sees and dumps the remainder
              # to the page as literal text.
              if section.settings.meta_field == 'client_groups'
                assign loc = entry.client_groups.value
              else
                assign loc = entry.type.value
              endif

              if section.settings.link_target == 'collection'
                assign url = entry.collection_url.value
              else
                assign url = entry.system.url
              endif

              assign bio = blank
              if section.settings.show_bio
                assign bio = entry.introduction.value
              endif
            -%}

            {%- capture facet_1_cell -%}
              {%- render 'club-instructor-field', entry: entry, field: f1 -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- capture facet_2_cell -%}
              {%- render 'club-instructor-field', entry: entry, field: f2 -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            {%- capture card_data -%}
              data-instructor-card
              data-name="{{ entry.name.value | escape }}"
              data-facet1="{{ facet_1_cell | escape }}"
              data-facet2="{{ facet_2_cell | escape }}"
            {%- endcapture -%}

            {%- render 'club-instructor-card',
              card_name: entry.name.value,
              card_cert: entry.certification.value,
              card_loc: loc,
              card_bio: bio,
              card_image: entry.picture.value,
              card_url: url,
              card_class: 'club-roster__item',
              card_sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 20vw, 44vw',
              card_data: card_data
            -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        </instructor-filter>

        {%- render 'pagination', paginate: paginate -%}
      {%- endpaginate -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Instructor roster",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reads the instructor metaobject directly. Replaces the paired list-metafield sections — no page metafield is involved, and there is no 50-entry cap."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Reads the our_team metaobject. The type handle is fixed in the section file because Shopify's paginate tag only accepts a static path — a setting here would silently do nothing."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "per_page",
      "min": 50,
      "max": 250,
      "step": 25,
      "label": "Entries per page",
      "default": 250,
      "info": "250 is the maximum. At 72 instructors everything fits on one page and no pagination controls appear. Do not set this below your roster size unless you want paging."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Ordering and visibility"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Both are blank by default, which reproduces the old behaviour exactly. Fill them in only after adding the matching fields to the metaobject definition."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sort_by",
      "label": "Sort by field",
      "info": "Field handle to order by, e.g. sort_order. Leave blank for the definition's own order. Use an INTEGER field — sorting a text field gives 1, 10, 11, 2. Verify the result against a known order before trusting it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "visible_field",
      "label": "Visibility field",
      "info": "Boolean field handle, e.g. visible. Only entries set to true are shown. Leave blank to show every entry. Without this, adding an entry publishes it immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Filtering"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Filters run in the browser against the cards already on the page — instant, no reload. Facet values are read from the entries themselves, so they always match the data. Because certification and type are free text, 'CASI 2' and 'CASI II' appear as two separate chips. Clean the entries, not this setting."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "enable_filter",
      "label": "Enable filtering",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "filter_by_name",
      "label": "Search by name",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "facet_1_field",
      "label": "Filter group 1 — field",
      "options": [
        { "value": "", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "certification", "label": "Certification" },
        { "value": "type", "label": "Type" },
        { "value": "client_groups", "label": "Client groups" }
      ],
      "default": "certification"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "facet_1_label",
      "label": "Filter group 1 — label",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the translated default for the chosen field."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "facet_2_field",
      "label": "Filter group 2 — field",
      "options": [
        { "value": "", "label": "None" },
        { "value": "certification", "label": "Certification" },
        { "value": "type", "label": "Type" },
        { "value": "client_groups", "label": "Client groups" }
      ],
      "default": "type"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "facet_2_label",
      "label": "Filter group 2 — label",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the translated default for the chosen field."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "columns",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 6,
      "step": 1,
      "label": "Columns (desktop)",
      "default": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_bio",
      "label": "Show introduction",
      "default": false,
      "info": "Off keeps the grid scannable. At 72 entries, bios make the page very long."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "meta_field",
      "label": "Meta line",
      "options": [
        { "value": "type", "label": "Type" },
        { "value": "client_groups", "label": "Client groups" }
      ],
      "default": "type"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "link_target",
      "label": "Card links to",
      "options": [
        { "value": "profile", "label": "Instructor profile page" },
        { "value": "collection", "label": "Their collection" }
      ],
      "default": "profile"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Leave blank on a page template — the page title above already acts as the heading. Filling both in produces two stacked titles."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "subheading",
      "label": "Subheading"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Color scheme",
      "default": "background-1"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Instructor roster"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
